  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">-	Fiji ICAC dedicating specific resources to supporting Pacific exchanges 
-	At least 20 corruption investigators/prosecutors/FIU members involved in capacity development 
-       At least 3 trainings organized
--      At least 10 CSO &amp; private sector participants report greater commitment to advocating for FOI</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2021">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">Some Pacific criminal justice stakeholders are highly capable but expertise not consistent across all levels specifically in relation to capacities for detection, investigation and prosecution of financial and corruption-related crimes; All PICS have police/public prosecutors/ICACs tasked with law enforcement re corruption but investigation &amp; prosecutions skills are very variable;

Vanuatu implementing FOI regime; Cook Islands, Fiji, Palau, PNG, Solomon Islands developing FOI laws. Fiji, PNG have RTI in their constitutions.</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">-  Fiji ICAC dedicating specific resources to supporting Pacific exchanges 
-	At least 15 corruption investigators/prosecutors/FIU members involved in capacity development 
-	At least 2 trainings organized
--  Capacity-building programme designed for civil society and private sector designed</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">-MOU drafted for cooperation between FICAC and SIICAC, being finalized
-A total of 60 participants (43 male; 17 female) from 10 PICs
-Two regional knowledge exchange events and four bilateral consultations/knowledge events held with Solomon Islands, Samoa, Tuvalu and Fiji on specific case study submissions reflecting specific country organizational weaknesses and challenges.
-Capacity building programme on right to information designed for civil society and private sector designed and TOT organized</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x2022;	MOU between SIICAC and FICAC finalized and at least 3 knowledge exchange events organized 
&#x2022;	At least 30 corruption investigators/prosecutors/FIU members involved in capacity development 
&#x2022;	At least 2 new regional trainings organized
&#x2022;	Capacity building programme implemented and 2 RTI prototypes designed and tested with users</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">MOU between SIICAC and FICAC finalized and agreed between both parties. The signing was due to take place at the end of November but was postponed to early January 2023. Knowledge provided by FICAC to SIICAC during at least three events (induction training, inter-institutional dialogue in SOI on anti-corruption of September 2022 and inter-institutional dialogue on integrity in SOI of May 2022).
More than 300 participants benefited from technical assistance and knowledge-sharing activities on anticorruption and transparency. 
19 trainings/knowledge-sharing/mentoring events. Topics covered included: Addressing
Corruption in the Pacific &#x2013; what has been tried, what has worked and what else might be done;
Disrupting Corruption: Stakeholder Management Webinar; Parallel Financial Investigations &amp; Asset
Recovery Corruption Proceeds; Evidence-based National Risk Assessment; Financial
Investigations Trainings; Corruption Prevention Training for Designated Non-Financial Businesses
&amp; Professions (DNFBPs) in Fiji (with regional access) and Solomon Islands, and Stakeholder Management: Whole of Society Approach to Anti-Corruption; ten-day direct mentoring for SOI FIU; direct technical advice to DPP SOI.
In cooperation with USP, capacity building programme implemented and 2 RTI prototypes developed. Under development is right to information e-course and continued RTI training.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
